# NewUnera — Notifications icon rails (filled glyphs)

**Scope:** [`NewUnera/notifications.html`](../NewUnera/notifications.html)

**Family:** Material Symbols Outlined (`viewBox="0 -960 960 960"`, `opsz` 24 paths), **FILL=1** exports only.

## Surfaces (all must use filled paths + `fill="currentColor"`; no strokes)

| Region | Notes |
|--------|--------|
| `#notification-list` `.notification-card-icon` | Type wells: transaction, system, listing, donation, remittance, verification |
| `#notificationPanel` `.notif-panel-header` | e.g. `close` / dismiss control SVGs — use filled `close` path from [`newunera-icons.mdc`](newunera-icons.mdc) §6 |
| `#notificationPanel` `.notif-list-wrapper` | `.notif-item-icon` type glyphs (JS: `PANEL_ICON_PATHS`) + row dismiss icon |
| `.notification-bell-btn` `.notif-bell-icon` | Canonical `notifications` slug from [`brand-style-guide.html`](../NewUnera/brand-style-guide.html) icon specimens |

## CSS guard (match implementation)

Scoped rules should enforce **fill-only** rendering and forbid accidental stroke styling:

```css
#notificationPanel svg,
.notification-bell-btn .notif-bell-icon,
#notification-list .notification-card-icon svg {
    fill: currentColor;
    stroke: none;
}
```

Do **not** add `stroke`, `stroke-width`, or `fill="none"` on these inline SVGs.

## Canonical slug → path source of truth

Align **type** icons with **filled** columns in `NewUnera/brand-style-guide.html` (Icon library table):

| Notification type | Material slug | FILL=1 reference |
|-------------------|---------------|-------------------|
| `transaction` | `paid` | First column (filled ring / inner disk) |
| `system` | `lock` | Second column (solid body) |
| `listing` | `home` | Filled home |
| `donation` | `favorite` | Filled heart |
| `remittance` | `payments` | Filled bill + card |
| `verification` | `verified` (shield + check) | Verified shield row |

Keep **`NOTIFICATION_ICONS`** (full `<svg>` for list cards) and **`PANEL_ICON_PATHS`** (`<path d="…">` only for the panel) **in sync** on every glyph change.

## Relation to global policy

This is an **exception** to the generic “micro-glyphs / small panel icons = FILL 0” hints in [`.cursor/rules/newunera-icons.mdc`](newunera-icons.mdc) §2 — notifications are a **dense finance-style rail** and use filled category glyphs by design.
